\label{chap:vsacse_lab_validation}

\section{Introduction}

The Venusian Sub-Surface Astrological Cryptographic Simulation Engine
(VS-ACSE), revision VS-ACSE-v4.0-REV2026, is a hardware-deterministic
planetary simulation framework designed to model mantle convection,
rift-flank widening, crustal relaxation, and cryptographically verified
state propagation under extreme dynamical conditions. This chapter presents
the complete laboratory validation of the VS-ACSE deterministic arithmetic
substrate, AVX2 SIMD execution pipeline, and ChaCha20/SHA3-256 telemetry
mesh across one hundred million execution cycles.

The objective of this validation campaign is to confirm that VS-ACSE
maintains absolute bit-level reproducibility, deterministic timing,
and cryptographically secure state evolution under controlled laboratory
conditions.

\section{Laboratory Test Bench Infrastructure}

All laboratory experiments were conducted on an isolated bare-metal
industrial controller configured to eliminate non-deterministic operating
system behavior. The following hardware and software constraints were
enforced:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Compute Node:} Dual-socket x86\_64 industrial controller
    with pinned CPU cores and disabled frequency scaling
    (\texttt{cpupower frequency-set -g performance}).
    \item \textbf{Memory Substrate:} Page-locked, pre-allocated static
    byte arrays ensuring zero heap allocation throughout execution.
    \item \textbf{Arithmetic Model:} Q16.16 fixed-point signed integers
    (32-bit), eliminating IEEE 754 floating-point drift.
    \item \textbf{Vector Execution Pipeline:} Inline AVX2 intrinsics
    operating on 8 parallel 32-bit lanes per \texttt{\_\_m256i} register.
    \item \textbf{Integrity Loop:} Continuous ChaCha20 stream cipher
    coupled with synchronous SHA3-256 hashing.
\end{itemize}

This configuration ensures that all observed behavior arises solely from
the VS-ACSE architecture, free from external nondeterministic influences.

